TEXT -288 -184 Left 4 ;Example 3.8: A normal transformer with U1/U2 = 230 V/46 V, lp/Is = 1 A/5 A, ukT = 10 % is connected\nas autotransformer with U1/U2 = 230 V/276 V. How much is the transfered apparent power\nand the primary short circuit current ?\n \nFor the normal transformer:\nSt=230V*1A=230VA\nIp(shorted)=I1N/ukT=1A/0.1A=10A\nFor the autotransformer:\nSd=St/(1-U1/U2)=230VA/(1-230V/276V)=1380VA(6*230VA) NOTE: If U1>U2 Sd=St/(1-U2/U1)\nIp=Sd/U1=1380VA/230V=6A\nukd=ukt*(1-U1/U2)=10%*(1-230V/276V)=1.67%(ukt/6) NOTE: If U1>U2 ukd=ukt*(1-U2/U1)\nIp(shorted)=Ip/ukd=6A/0.0167=360A
